        {
          "component": "callout",
          "track": "overlay",
          "from": 2,
          "duration": 12,
          "props": {
            "kicker": "The Thermal Limit",
            "text": "1,000 watts dissipated in a piece of silicon the size of a postage stamp.",
            "position": "bottom-right"
          }
        }
      ],
      "narration": {
        "src": "narration/ai-gold-rush/sc15.mp3",
        "text": "When electricity enters a semiconductor chip, almost all of it is converted directly into heat. As modern accelerators push past one thousand watts per processor die, the laws of thermodynamics impose an inescapable physical ceiling.",
        "gainDb": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sc16",
      "chapterId": "ch4",
      "transitionIn": {
        "type": "cross-zoom",
        "duration": 0.7
      },
      "note": "",
      "layers": [
        {
          "component": "backdrop",
          "track": "background",
          "props": {
            "glow": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "component": "diagram",
          "track": "main",
          "props": {
            "parts": [
              {
                "x": 0.5,
                "y": 0.35,
                "label": "Accelerator Die",
                "sub": "1,000 W thermal output",
                "side": "right"
              },
              {
                "x": 0.38,
                "y": 0.55,
                "label": "Air Cooling Limit",
                "sub": "Thermal boundary reached",
                "side": "left"
              },
              {
                "x": 0.62,
                "y": 0.72,
                "label": "Fan Power Spike",
                "sub": "Consumes >30% server power",
                "side": "right"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "narration": {
        "src": "narration/ai-gold-rush/sc16.mp3",
        "text": "Air cooling—the historical practice of blowing chilled air across aluminum heat sinks—has reached its theoretical limit. Air simply cannot absorb heat quickly enough from modern silicon dies without requiring fans that consume more power than the chips themselves.",
        "gainDb": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sc17",
      "chapterId": "ch4",
      "transitionIn": {
